{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794914521789,"sessionID":"ses_e16c29ae3ffeLmKp3aWafWpYBG","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_f33193d98b4b474d8edcd3af","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Analyze parcels shipping code","prompt":"Explore this repository thoroughly enough to answer these four questions about the parcels/shipping code. Do not modify files. Questions: (1) From what order value is shipping free, and how can that value be changed without editing code? (2) What happens to an order heavier than a single parcel may be? (3) Which carrier is used when nothing is configured, and how is another one chosen? (4) How is the delivery date worked out for an order placed Friday at 17:00? Does it account for weekends and public holidays? Return exact implementation details, configuration mechanisms, and precise relative file paths plus exact line numbers/ranges for every relevant claim. Inspect code and tests as needed. Thoroughness: very thorough.","subagent_type":"explore","command":"Answer the four parcels questions in the repository and cite exact code locations"},"output":"<task id=\"ses_e16c27b1effeUp6h9ge63Rk8Io\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\n## Repository root and source map\n\nAll relative paths below are rooted at:\n\n`/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/answer-questions/opencode-1/repo`\n\n| Relative path | Absolute path |\n|---|---|\n| `parcels/settings.py` | `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/answer-questions/opencode-1/repo/parcels/settings.py` |\n| `parcels/quote.py` | `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/answer-questions/opencode-1/repo/parcels/quote.py` |\n| `parcels/packing.py` | `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/answer-questions/opencode-1/repo/parcels/packing.py` |\n| `parcels/carriers.py` | `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/answer-questions/opencode-1/repo/parcels/carriers.py` |\n| `parcels/delivery.py` | `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/answer-questions/opencode-1/repo/parcels/delivery.py` |\n| `parcels/__main__.py` | `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/answer-questions/opencode-1/repo/parcels/__main__.py` |\n| `tests/test_parcels.py` | `/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/answer-questions/opencode-1/repo/tests/test_parcels.py` |\n\n## 1. Free-shipping threshold and how to change it\n\n**Shipping is free at an order value of €60.00 or more**, where the order value is the amount **after discounts** and the destination is inside the EU.\n\n- The default is `Decimal(\"60.00\")`:\n\n  ```python\n  FREE_SHIPPING_FROM = Decimal(os.environ.get(\"PARCELS_FREE_FROM\", \"60.00\"))\n  ```\n\n  `parcels/settings.py:14-15`\n\n- The comparison is inclusive:\n\n  ```python\n  if order_value >= FREE_SHIPPING_FROM:\n      return Decimal(\"0.00\")\n  ```\n\n  `parcels/quote.py:31-32`\n\n- The function documentation explicitly says the order value is “euros (after discounts)” (`parcels/quote.py:25-26`), and the setting’s comment says the free-shipping rule is “inside the EU” (`parcels/settings.py:14`).\n\n### Changing it without editing code\n\nSet the `PARCELS_FREE_FROM` environment variable before starting the process, for example:\n\n```bash\nPARCELS_FREE_FROM=75.00 python -m parcels 45.00 3.2 DE\n```\n\nThe value is parsed as a `Decimal`, so values such as `\"60.00\"`, `\"60\"`, or `\"75.50\"` are accepted (`parcels/settings.py:15`).\n\nThe environment is read **once, at import time** (`parcels/settings.py:1`). Therefore, changing the process environment after `parcels.settings` has already been imported does not update the threshold; the application/worker must be restarted or the module reloaded.\n\n### EU restriction\n\nThe destination is checked before the free-shipping test:\n\n```python\ncountry = country.upper()\nif country not in EU:\n    raise CannotShip(f\"we do not ship to {country}\")\n```\n\n`parcels/quote.py:28-30`\n\nThe supported EU country set is defined at `parcels/carriers.py:22-24`. Consequently, a high-value order to a non-EU destination is rejected rather than treated as free shipping.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Orders heavier than one parcel\n\nThere is no single-parcel-only restriction. A paid order over the parcel limit is divided into several parcels.\n\n### Parcel limit and splitting algorithm\n\n- A single parcel may weigh at most **31.5 kg**:\n\n  ```python\n  MAX_PARCEL_KG = Decimal(\"31.5\")\n  ```\n\n  `parcels/settings.py:17`\n\n- The parcel count is the smallest integer that can keep every parcel at or below that limit:\n\n  ```python\n  count = max(1, math.ceil(total_kg / MAX_PARCEL_KG))\n  ```\n\n  `parcels/packing.py:20`\n\n- All parcels are given the same weight. The per-parcel weight is rounded **up to the next gram**:\n\n  ```python\n  each = (total_kg / count).quantize(\n      Decimal(\"0.001\"), rounding=\"ROUND_CEILING\"\n  )\n  return [each] * count\n  ```\n\n  `parcels/packing.py:21-22`\n\nThus, for example, **70 kg becomes three parcels of 23.334 kg each**. This behavior is documented at `parcels/packing.py:11-16` and tested at `tests/test_parcels.py:11-12`.\n\nThere is no maximum total order weight in the implementation; an arbitrarily heavy positive order is split into more parcels. Only a non-positive weight is rejected:\n\n```python\nif total_kg <= 0:\n    raise ValueError(\"an order weighs something\")\n```\n\n`parcels/packing.py:18-19`\n\n### How split parcels affect the price\n\nShipping charges are calculated **per parcel**, then summed:\n\n```python\nreturn sum(\n    (parcel_price(w, country) for w in parcel_weights(weight_kg)),\n    Decimal(\"0.00\"),\n)\n```\n\n`parcels/quote.py:33`\n\nEach parcel’s price consists of:\n\n- a fixed base charge,\n- a charge per **started whole kilogram**,\n- plus the EU surcharge for destinations outside the Netherlands.\n\n```python\nprice = tariff.base + tariff.per_kg * math.ceil(weight_kg)\nif country != \"NL\":\n    price += tariff.eu_surcharge\n```\n\n`parcels/quote.py:17-22`\n\nFor example, the default PostNL parcel of 23.334 kg would be charged as 24 started kilograms (`math.ceil(23.334) == 24`). The carrier tariffs are:\n\n| Carrier | Base per parcel | Per started kg | Non-NL EU surcharge per parcel |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| DHL | €4.95 | €0.40 | €6.00 |\n| UPS | €6.50 | €0.30 | €5.00 |\n| PostNL | €4.10 | €0.45 | €7.25 |\n\nSource: `parcels/carriers.py:16-20`.\n\nOne qualification: if the order already qualifies for free shipping, `shipping_cost` returns €0 **before** calling the packing function (`parcels/quote.py:31-33`), so packing is irrelevant to that quote.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Default carrier and choosing another carrier\n\n### Default\n\n**PostNL is used when nothing is configured.**\n\n```python\nCARRIER = os.environ.get(\"PARCELS_CARRIER\", \"postnl\").lower()\n```\n\n`parcels/settings.py:10`\n\n### Choosing another carrier\n\nSet the `PARCELS_CARRIER` environment variable before starting the process:\n\n```bash\nPARCELS_CARRIER=dhl python -m parcels 45.00 3.2 DE\n```\n\nor:\n\n```bash\nPARCELS_CARRIER=ups python -m parcels 45.00 3.2 DE\n```\n\nThe allowed carrier names are:\n\n```python\nCARRIERS = (\"dhl\", \"ups\", \"postnl\")\n```\n\n`parcels/settings.py:8`\n\nThe environment value is lowercased, so values such as `DHL` are also accepted (`parcels/settings.py:10`). An unsupported value is not silently replaced with the default; it raises a `RuntimeError` during import:\n\n```python\nif CARRIER not in CARRIERS:\n    raise RuntimeError(\n        f\"PARCELS_CARRIER must be one of {', '.join(CARRIERS)}, \"\n        f\"not {CARRIER!r}\"\n    )\n```\n\n`parcels/settings.py:11-12`\n\nAs with the free-shipping setting, this is import-time configuration (`parcels/settings.py:1`), so the process must be restarted/reloaded after changing it.\n\nThe selected carrier determines which tariff is used:\n\n```python\ntariff = TARIFFS[CARRIER]\n```\n\n`parcels/quote.py:17-19`\n\nThe command-line interface has no carrier option; it accepts only order value, weight, and country (`parcels/__main__.py:13-24`).\n\n---\n\n## 4. Delivery date for an order placed Friday at 17:00\n\nThere is no single delivery date without a destination country, because transit time is country-dependent.\n\n### Algorithm\n\n1. The initial date is the order date.\n2. At or after **15:00**, handling starts from the next calendar day.\n3. Transit days are added according to destination.\n4. One additional handling day is added.\n5. Saturdays and Sundays are skipped.\n6. Public holidays are **not** skipped.\n\nThe constants are:\n\n```python\nTRANSIT_DAYS = {\"NL\": 1, \"BE\": 2, \"DE\": 2, \"LU\": 2}\nDEFAULT_TRANSIT_DAYS = 4\nCUTOFF_HOUR = 15\n```\n\n`parcels/delivery.py:9-11`\n\nThe handling period is one working day:\n\n```python\nHANDLING_DAYS = 1\n```\n\n`parcels/settings.py:18`\n\nThe calculation is:\n\n```python\ndef delivery_date(ordered: datetime, country: str) -> date:\n    start = ordered.date()\n    if ordered.hour >= CUTOFF_HOUR:\n        start += timedelta(days=1)\n    transit = TRANSIT_DAYS.get(country.upper(), DEFAULT_TRANSIT_DAYS)\n    return add_working_days(start, HANDLING_DAYS + transit)\n```\n\n`parcels/delivery.py:25-30`\n\nThe cutoff test uses only the hour. Therefore, **15:00 itself** already moves processing to the next day, and Friday at 17:00 does the same (`parcels/delivery.py:27-28`).\n\n### Friday at 17:00 result\n\nBecause the order is after the cutoff, the starting point becomes **Saturday**. The weekend-skipping function then advances one calendar day at a time, counting only Monday–Friday as working days:\n\n```python\nwhile days > 0:\n    current += timedelta(days=1)\n    if current.weekday() < 5:\n        days -= 1\n```\n\n`parcels/delivery.py:17-22`\n\nThe resulting date is therefore:\n\n| Destination | Transit days | Total working days counted | Delivery date |\n|---|---:|---:|---|\n| `NL` | 1 | 2 handling/transit days | **Tuesday of the following week** |\n| `BE`, `DE`, `LU` | 2 | 3 handling/transit days | **Wednesday of the following week** |\n| Every other destination, including other EU countries | 4 | 5 handling/transit days | **Friday of the following week** |\n\nThe destination lookup and fallback are at `parcels/delivery.py:29`; the combination with the one handling day is at `parcels/delivery.py:30`. The default-four-day behavior applies directly if `delivery_date` is called for another country, although the normal shipping flow rejects non-EU destinations first (`parcels/quote.py:28-30`).\n\nFor example, for the README’s `DE` destination, a Friday 17:00 order would be dated **Wednesday of the following week**.\n\n### Weekends and public holidays\n\n- **Weekends are accounted for.** The docstring explicitly says Saturdays and Sundays are skipped, and the implementation checks `weekday() < 5` (`parcels/delivery.py:14-22`).\n- **Public holidays are not accounted for.** The same docstring explicitly says “holidays are not” (`parcels/delivery.py:15`). There is no holiday calendar, holiday list, or country-specific holiday provider. A public holiday falling Monday–Friday is therefore treated as an ordinary working day and consumes one of the counted days, potentially producing an optimistic delivery date.\n- The tests corroborate weekend handling: Friday plus one working day becomes Monday, and a Thursday 16:00 Netherlands order becomes the following Tuesday (`tests/test_parcels.py:19-21`). There is no public-holiday test or holiday data in the repository.\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_e16c29ae3ffeLmKp3aWafWpYBG","sessionId":"ses_e16c27b1effeUp6h9ge63Rk8Io","model":{"modelID":"minimax/minimax-m3.1-flash","providerID":"openrouter"},"truncated":false},"title":"Analyze parcels shipping code","time":{"start":1794914485481,"end":1794914521783}},"id":"prt_1e93d828d00160KZ7xVfzuJhW0","sessionID":"ses_e16c29ae3ffeLmKp3aWafWpYBG","messageID":"msg_1e93d708a001LadyHK6uTIUmkj"}}
