er discounts\" is key. Inside EU maybe relevant. Mention.\n\nQ2:\n\"single parcel max 31.5 kg. It is split into ceil(total/31.5) (min1) parcels, equal weight rounded up to next gram. Example 70 -> 3 x23.334. Shipping quote charges each parcel separately because sum. Non-positive rejected. No total cap.\" Need be careful: Does split into ceil ensure each at most? Quantize ROUND_CEILING could theoretically exceed max due rounding? Let's inspect. For total e.g 31.500001, count 2, each 15.750001. Fine. For values exact multiple and gram rounding? e.g 63 -> count 2, 31.5. e.g 63.001 count3. Max <= 31.5 likely. Could state.\n\"Shipping quote charges each separately\" cite quote:33. The question might only ask what happens to order heavier than single parcel; enough.\n\"each parcel's shipping price is included\" yes.\nPotential free shipping case: if qualifies free, returns 0 before packing, but order still physically split? Packing only quote. Avoid overcomplication. Say when shipping is charged, quote sums each parcel. Good.\n\nQ3:\ndefault PostNL. Configure env PARCELS_CARRIER=dhl or ups, lowercased. Import-time. Invalid error. Cite settings. \"Tariff from TARIFFS[CARRIER]\" quote. Good.\n\nQ4:\nDetailed algorithm. Friday at 17 after cutoff, processing starts Saturday. Add one handling day + country transit, skipping Sat/Sun. For NL Tuesday following week; BE/DE/LU Wed; other countries default 5 workdays -> Friday. Public holidays not considered. Include citations:\n- transit map/default/cutoff delivery.py:9-11\n- cutoff start and add days delivery.py:25-30\n- handling days settings:18\n- add workdays and holiday doc delivery.py:14-22\nCould include citations to tests test_parcels.py:19-21.\nPotential subtlety: public holidays \"Does it account for weekends and public holidays?\" explicitly answer weekends yes, public holidays no. Could state a weekday public holiday is treated as working day.\nOne concern: \"order placed on a Friday at 17:00\" no country. We need point