{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794914539498,"sessionID":"ses_e16c29ae3ffeLmKp3aWafWpYBG","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_224dc2b4ab1e40618938435c","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Answers about the parcels code\n\n## Q1\n\nShipping is free for EU orders whose value, after discounts, is **€60.00 or more**. The default threshold is `FREE_SHIPPING_FROM = Decimal(\"60.00\")`, and the comparison is inclusive (`order_value >= FREE_SHIPPING_FROM`). Non-EU destinations are rejected before the free-shipping check. (`parcels/settings.py:14-15`, `parcels/quote.py:25-32`)\n\nThe threshold can be changed without editing code by setting the `PARCELS_FREE_FROM` environment variable before starting the process, for example `PARCELS_FREE_FROM=75.00`. Settings are read from the environment once at import, so the application must be restarted (or the module reloaded) for the new value to take effect. (`parcels/settings.py:1-15`)\n\n## Q2\n\nAn order heavier than **31.5 kg** is not rejected: it is divided into the smallest whole number of parcels needed to keep each parcel within that limit. The parcels have equal weights, rounded up to the next gram; for example, 70 kg becomes three parcels of 23.334 kg. There is no maximum total order weight in this implementation, though a non-positive weight is invalid. (`parcels/settings.py:17`, `parcels/packing.py:11-22`)\n\nWhen the order is not eligible for free shipping, shipping is calculated separately for every resulting parcel and the parcel prices are added together. (`parcels/quote.py:17-22`, `parcels/quote.py:33`)\n\n## Q3\n\nThe default carrier is **PostNL**. Another carrier is selected without editing code by setting `PARCELS_CARRIER` to `dhl`, `ups`, or `postnl` before starting the process, for example `PARCELS_CARRIER=dhl`. The value is lower-cased; an unsupported value raises a `RuntimeError`. As with the other settings, the environment is read at import time, so a running process must be restarted to use a change. (`parcels/settings.py:1-12`)\n\nThe configured carrier is used to select its tariff when calculating the price. (`parcels/quote.py:17-19`, `parcels/carriers.py:16-20`)\n\n## Q4\n\nThe result depends on the destination country. An order placed at 17:00 is after the 15:00 cutoff, so processing starts on the next calendar day—Saturday for a Friday order. The calculator then adds one handling day plus the destination's transit days, counting only Monday through Friday as working days. (`parcels/delivery.py:9-11`, `parcels/delivery.py:25-30`, `parcels/settings.py:18`)\n\nFor a Friday order, the resulting delivery dates are:\n\n- **NL:** Tuesday of the following week (one transit day).\n- **BE, DE, or LU:** Wednesday of the following week (two transit days).\n- **Any other country:** Friday of the following week (the default four transit days). (`parcels/delivery.py:9-10`, `parcels/delivery.py:29-30`)\n\n**Weekends are accounted for:** the date calculation skips Saturday and Sunday. **Public holidays are not accounted for:** there is no holiday calendar, and a public holiday on a weekday is treated as a normal working day. (`parcels/delivery.py:14-22`)\n","filePath":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/answer-questions/opencode-1/repo/ANSWERS.md"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-alexander--claude-spares-spare-IwZtqC/50e3bfb1-34ed-4585-ad26-c678e31a5e93/scratchpad/agents-out2/amend-opencode/answer-questions/opencode-1/repo/ANSWERS.md","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"ANSWERS.md","time":{"start":1794914539484,"end":1794914539494}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Need write content. Let's ensure wording technically exact.\n\nQ1:\n\"Free shipping applies when order_value >= threshold; default threshold €60.00. order value after discounts. inside EU only because non EU rejects.\"\n\"change env variable PARCELS_FREE_FROM=75.00 before starting application; imported once, so restart needed.\"\nCite settings 1,14-15, quote 25-32.\n\nQ2:\n\"max 31.5. count ceil, weights equal rounded up to gram. 70 =>3x23.334. nonpositive raises. No maximum total. When paid, shipping each parcel summed.\" Note wording \"an order that is heavier than a single parcel may be\" likely says heavier than one parcel may be. Need no mention no max perhaps useful. Could say \"There is no special rejection merely because it is heavy.\" This addresses. But is no max total definitely yes. packing accepts any positive Decimal; count arbitrarily many. Good.\nPotential decimal huge; no max.\nCite settings17, packing11-22, quote33.\n\nQ3:\n\"postnl default; PARCELS_CARRIER env, lowercased; values dhl ups postnl; invalid raises RuntimeError at import; change before process start/restart. Selected tariff.\" Cite settings 8-12 and quote17-19.\n\nQ4:\nMaybe handling day semantics: \"handling starts from next day\" but then add working days starts by incrementing. At order 17:00 Friday, start is Sat. add working days counts Mon as handling, etc. NL 2 = Mon Tue. Great.\nOne subtle issue: \"delivery date is worked out for an order placed on Friday at 17:00\" At 17 cutoff start Sat. But `add_working_days` always adds one calendar day before counting. So yes.\n\"other EU destinations default 4 transit days\", even though EU map only listed NL BE DE LU and fallback all others. Normal shipping supports all EU. Great.\n\"BE DE LU\" transit2. Could list.\nCitations: delivery 9-11,25-30; settings18; delivery14-22.\nCould cite tests 19-21 for weekend. Public holidays source docstring explicitly not. Good.\nNeed perhaps say minutes ignored? Not needed.\nNo comments constraint irrelevant.\n\nLet's write.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1e93e53d2001LVez8W01kURvl5","sessionID":"ses_e16c29ae3ffeLmKp3aWafWpYBG","messageID":"msg_1e93e43cf001F9rbgXMuxBIV0m"}}
